window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/a094-ea36dceccffad30b.json"]={sha256:"ea36dceccffad30bf0d674f22121fd5cc5941d18ab7c43c8fec09b796d284619",value:{"id":"a094","title":"晶圓缺陷分類與良率分析","titleEn":"Wafer defect classification and yield analysis","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從缺陷單位、混淆矩陣到改善驗證：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Defect units and Confusion matrix to Improvement verification: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["缺陷單位","人工真值","空間模式","良率模型"],"labelsEn":["Defect units","Reference labels","Spatial patterns","Yield model"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a094-stage01","order":1,"title":"缺陷單位 → 檢出門檻","titleEn":"Defect units to Detection threshold","description":"把「缺陷單位」「座標配準」「檢出門檻」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Defect units, Coordinate registration, Detection threshold.","steps":[{"id":"a094-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"缺陷單位：建立模型","titleEn":"Defect units: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects.","instruction":"分開影像缺陷、實體缺陷與失效晶粒三種計數。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate image detections, physical defects and failed dies. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷；同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察。","observationEn":"Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects; One defect may appear on several layers.","failure":"若採用「把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating detection count with failed-die count\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「缺陷單位」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷。","checkEn":"Submit the Defect units diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-01-k1","title":"缺陷單位／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defect units / Physics and model","text":"機制：多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷。","textEn":"Mechanism: Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects."},{"id":"a094-v8-01-k2","title":"缺陷單位／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defect units / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating detection count with failed-die count."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「缺陷單位」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Defect units, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷","把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數","直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像"],"optionsEn":["Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects","Equating detection count with failed-die count","Overlaying maps without checking mirroring"],"answer":0,"explanation":"多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-01"],"title":"缺陷單位：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Defect units: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating detection count with failed-die count.","instruction":"接續前一步「缺陷單位」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Defect units artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating detection count with failed-die count\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: One defect may appear on several layers. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷；同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察。","observationEn":"Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects; One defect may appear on several layers.","failure":"若採用「把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating detection count with failed-die count\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「缺陷單位」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Defect units, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"One defect may appear on several layers\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-02-k1","title":"缺陷單位／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defect units / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: One defect may appear on several layers."},{"id":"a094-v8-02-k2","title":"缺陷單位／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defect units / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數」與「多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating detection count with failed-die count\" is not equivalent to \"Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「缺陷單位」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Defect units?","options":["直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像","同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察","把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數"],"optionsEn":["Overlaying maps without checking mirroring","One defect may appear on several layers","Equating detection count with failed-die count"],"answer":1,"explanation":"同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"One defect may appear on several layers. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-02"],"title":"座標配準：建立模型","titleEn":"Coordinate registration: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence.","instruction":"用晶圓缺口和三個不對稱標记對齊兩站地圖。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Register two maps with a notch and asymmetric marks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應；鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤。","observationEn":"Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence; Mirror errors break causal tracing.","failure":"若採用「直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Overlaying maps without checking mirroring\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「座標配準」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應。","checkEn":"Submit the Coordinate registration diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-03-k1","title":"座標配準／物理與模型","titleEn":"Coordinate registration / Physics and model","text":"機制：翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應。","textEn":"Mechanism: Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence."},{"id":"a094-v8-03-k2","title":"座標配準／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Coordinate registration / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Overlaying maps without checking mirroring."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「座標配準」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Coordinate registration, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像","檢出越多就必然代表製程更差","翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應"],"optionsEn":["Overlaying maps without checking mirroring","Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing","Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence"],"answer":2,"explanation":"翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-03"],"title":"座標配準：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Coordinate registration: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Overlaying maps without checking mirroring.","instruction":"接續前一步「座標配準」成果，先指出錯誤主張「直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Coordinate registration artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Overlaying maps without checking mirroring\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Mirror errors break causal tracing. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應；鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤。","observationEn":"Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence; Mirror errors break causal tracing.","failure":"若採用「直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Overlaying maps without checking mirroring\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「座標配準」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Coordinate registration, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Mirror errors break causal tracing\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-04-k1","title":"座標配準／物理與模型","titleEn":"Coordinate registration / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Mirror errors break causal tracing."},{"id":"a094-v8-04-k2","title":"座標配準／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Coordinate registration / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像」與「翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Overlaying maps without checking mirroring\" is not equivalent to \"Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「座標配準」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Coordinate registration?","options":["鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤","直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像","檢出越多就必然代表製程更差"],"optionsEn":["Mirror errors break causal tracing","Overlaying maps without checking mirroring","Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing"],"answer":0,"explanation":"鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mirror errors break causal tracing. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-04"],"title":"檢出門檻：建立模型","titleEn":"Detection threshold: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms.","instruction":"以假設真缺陷和背景分布繪製門檻取捨。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Plot a hypothetical detection/background threshold tradeoff. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警；ROC 比較需相同參考標籤。","observationEn":"Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms; ROC comparisons need the same reference labels.","failure":"若採用「檢出越多就必然代表製程更差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「檢出門檻」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警。","checkEn":"Submit the Detection threshold diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-05-k1","title":"檢出門檻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Detection threshold / Physics and model","text":"機制：降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警。","textEn":"Mechanism: Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms."},{"id":"a094-v8-05-k2","title":"檢出門檻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Detection threshold / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「檢出越多就必然代表製程更差」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「檢出門檻」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Detection threshold, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類","降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警","檢出越多就必然代表製程更差"],"optionsEn":["Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes","Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms","Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing"],"answer":1,"explanation":"降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-05"],"title":"檢出門檻：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Detection threshold: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「檢出越多就必然代表製程更差」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing.","instruction":"接續前一步「檢出門檻」成果，先指出錯誤主張「檢出越多就必然代表製程更差」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：ROC 比較需相同參考標籤。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Detection threshold artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: ROC comparisons need the same reference labels. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警；ROC 比較需相同參考標籤。","observationEn":"Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms; ROC comparisons need the same reference labels.","failure":"若採用「檢出越多就必然代表製程更差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「檢出門檻」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「ROC 比較需相同參考標籤」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Detection threshold, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"ROC comparisons need the same reference labels\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-06-k1","title":"檢出門檻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Detection threshold / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：ROC 比較需相同參考標籤。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: ROC comparisons need the same reference labels."},{"id":"a094-v8-06-k2","title":"檢出門檻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Detection threshold / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「檢出越多就必然代表製程更差」與「降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing\" is not equivalent to \"Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「檢出門檻」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Detection threshold?","options":["檢出越多就必然代表製程更差","強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類","ROC 比較需相同參考標籤"],"optionsEn":["Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing","Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes","ROC comparisons need the same reference labels"],"answer":2,"explanation":"ROC 比較需相同參考標籤；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"ROC comparisons need the same reference labels. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a094-stage02","order":2,"title":"人工真值 → 尺寸與危害","titleEn":"Reference labels to Size and criticality","description":"把「人工真值」「混淆矩陣」「尺寸與危害」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Reference labels, Confusion matrix, Size and criticality.","steps":[{"id":"a094-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-06"],"title":"人工真值：建立模型","titleEn":"Reference labels: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「參考標籤本身也有不確定性」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Reference labels themselves have uncertainty.","instruction":"建立雙人複核及爭議標籤，保留未知類別。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Create dual review/disagreement labels and retain unknowns. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"參考標籤本身也有不確定性；審查者一致率可量化標籤品質。","observationEn":"Reference labels themselves have uncertainty; Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality.","failure":"若採用「強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「人工真值」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：參考標籤本身也有不確定性。","checkEn":"Submit the Reference labels diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Reference labels themselves have uncertainty.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-07-k1","title":"人工真值／物理與模型","titleEn":"Reference labels / Physics and model","text":"機制：參考標籤本身也有不確定性。","textEn":"Mechanism: Reference labels themselves have uncertainty."},{"id":"a094-v8-07-k2","title":"人工真值／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Reference labels / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「人工真值」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Reference labels, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["參考標籤本身也有不確定性","強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類","只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到"],"optionsEn":["Reference labels themselves have uncertainty","Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes","Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture"],"answer":0,"explanation":"參考標籤本身也有不確定性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Reference labels themselves have uncertainty. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-07"],"title":"人工真值：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Reference labels: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes.","instruction":"接續前一步「人工真值」成果，先指出錯誤主張「強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：審查者一致率可量化標籤品質。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Reference labels artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"參考標籤本身也有不確定性；審查者一致率可量化標籤品質。","observationEn":"Reference labels themselves have uncertainty; Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality.","failure":"若採用「強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「人工真值」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「審查者一致率可量化標籤品質」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Reference labels, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-08-k1","title":"人工真值／物理與模型","titleEn":"Reference labels / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：審查者一致率可量化標籤品質。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality."},{"id":"a094-v8-08-k2","title":"人工真值／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Reference labels / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類」與「參考標籤本身也有不確定性」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes\" is not equivalent to \"Reference labels themselves have uncertainty\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「人工真值」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Reference labels?","options":["只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到","審查者一致率可量化標籤品質","強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類"],"optionsEn":["Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture","Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality","Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"審查者一致率可量化標籤品質；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-08"],"title":"混淆矩陣：建立模型","titleEn":"Confusion matrix: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data.","instruction":"用假設刮傷、粒子與正常樣本算每類精確率召回率。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compute per-class precision/recall for scratches, particles and normal samples. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效；精確率受類別盛行率影響。","observationEn":"Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data; Precision depends on class prevalence.","failure":"若採用「只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「混淆矩陣」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效。","checkEn":"Submit the Confusion matrix diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-09-k1","title":"混淆矩陣／物理與模型","titleEn":"Confusion matrix / Physics and model","text":"機制：不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效。","textEn":"Mechanism: Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data."},{"id":"a094-v8-09-k2","title":"混淆矩陣／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Confusion matrix / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「混淆矩陣」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Confusion matrix, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到","最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命","不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效"],"optionsEn":["Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture","Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal","Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-09"],"title":"混淆矩陣：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Confusion matrix: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture.","instruction":"接續前一步「混淆矩陣」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：精確率受類別盛行率影響。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Confusion matrix artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Precision depends on class prevalence. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效；精確率受類別盛行率影響。","observationEn":"Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data; Precision depends on class prevalence.","failure":"若採用「只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「混淆矩陣」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「精確率受類別盛行率影響」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Confusion matrix, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Precision depends on class prevalence\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-10-k1","title":"混淆矩陣／物理與模型","titleEn":"Confusion matrix / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：精確率受類別盛行率影響。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Precision depends on class prevalence."},{"id":"a094-v8-10-k2","title":"混淆矩陣／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Confusion matrix / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到」與「不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture\" is not equivalent to \"Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「混淆矩陣」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Confusion matrix?","options":["精確率受類別盛行率影響","只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到","最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命"],"optionsEn":["Precision depends on class prevalence","Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture","Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal"],"answer":0,"explanation":"精確率受類別盛行率影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Precision depends on class prevalence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-10"],"title":"尺寸與危害：建立模型","titleEn":"Size and criticality: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Criticality depends on defect position and layout.","instruction":"將缺陷投到線距及接觸孔版圖，判讀短路與開路風險。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Overlay defects on spacing/contact layouts and assess bridge/open risk. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形；接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命。","observationEn":"Criticality depends on defect position and layout; Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal.","failure":"若採用「最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「尺寸與危害」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形。","checkEn":"Submit the Size and criticality diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Criticality depends on defect position and layout.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-11-k1","title":"尺寸與危害／物理與模型","titleEn":"Size and criticality / Physics and model","text":"機制：缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形。","textEn":"Mechanism: Criticality depends on defect position and layout."},{"id":"a094-v8-11-k2","title":"尺寸與危害／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Size and criticality / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「尺寸與危害」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Size and criticality, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備","缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形","最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命"],"optionsEn":["Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring","Criticality depends on defect position and layout","Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Criticality depends on defect position and layout. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-11"],"title":"尺寸與危害：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Size and criticality: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal.","instruction":"接續前一步「尺寸與危害」成果，先指出錯誤主張「最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Size and criticality artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形；接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命。","observationEn":"Criticality depends on defect position and layout; Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal.","failure":"若採用「最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「尺寸與危害」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Size and criticality, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-12-k1","title":"尺寸與危害／物理與模型","titleEn":"Size and criticality / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal."},{"id":"a094-v8-12-k2","title":"尺寸與危害／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Size and criticality / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命」與「缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal\" is not equivalent to \"Criticality depends on defect position and layout\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「尺寸與危害」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Size and criticality?","options":["最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命","看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備","接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命"],"optionsEn":["Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal","Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring","Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal"],"answer":2,"explanation":"接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a094-stage03","order":3,"title":"空間模式 → 缺陷增量","titleEn":"Spatial patterns to Defect adders","description":"把「空間模式」「時間追溯」「缺陷增量」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Spatial patterns, Temporal genealogy, Defect adders.","steps":[{"id":"a094-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-12"],"title":"空間模式：建立模型","titleEn":"Spatial patterns: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness.","instruction":"比較邊環、刮痕與隨機點的假設地圖。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical edge-ring, scratch and random maps. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果；晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式。","observationEn":"Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness; Edge exclusion changes visible patterns.","failure":"若採用「看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「空間模式」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果。","checkEn":"Submit the Spatial patterns diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-13-k1","title":"空間模式／物理與模型","titleEn":"Spatial patterns / Physics and model","text":"機制：空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果。","textEn":"Mechanism: Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness."},{"id":"a094-v8-13-k2","title":"空間模式／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Spatial patterns / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「空間模式」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Spatial patterns, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果","看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備","只看最後一台設備便確定來源"],"optionsEn":["Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness","Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring","Blaming only the final tool"],"answer":0,"explanation":"空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-13"],"title":"空間模式：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Spatial patterns: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring.","instruction":"接續前一步「空間模式」成果，先指出錯誤主張「看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Spatial patterns artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Edge exclusion changes visible patterns. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果；晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式。","observationEn":"Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness; Edge exclusion changes visible patterns.","failure":"若採用「看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「空間模式」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Spatial patterns, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Edge exclusion changes visible patterns\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-14-k1","title":"空間模式／物理與模型","titleEn":"Spatial patterns / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Edge exclusion changes visible patterns."},{"id":"a094-v8-14-k2","title":"空間模式／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Spatial patterns / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備」與「空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring\" is not equivalent to \"Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「空間模式」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Spatial patterns?","options":["只看最後一台設備便確定來源","晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式","看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備"],"optionsEn":["Blaming only the final tool","Edge exclusion changes visible patterns","Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring"],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Edge exclusion changes visible patterns. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-14"],"title":"時間追溯：建立模型","titleEn":"Temporal genealogy: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone.","instruction":"將缺陷發生片號連到設備、腔室與保養時刻。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Link defect wafer IDs to tools, chambers and maintenance times. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力；混批會破壞腔室追溯。","observationEn":"Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone; Mixed lots can break chamber traceability.","failure":"若採用「只看最後一台設備便確定來源」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Blaming only the final tool\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「時間追溯」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力。","checkEn":"Submit the Temporal genealogy diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-15-k1","title":"時間追溯／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temporal genealogy / Physics and model","text":"機制：共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力。","textEn":"Mechanism: Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone."},{"id":"a094-v8-15-k2","title":"時間追溯／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temporal genealogy / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看最後一台設備便確定來源」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Blaming only the final tool."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「時間追溯」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Temporal genealogy, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只看最後一台設備便確定來源","直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數","共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力"],"optionsEn":["Blaming only the final tool","Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders","Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone"],"answer":2,"explanation":"共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-15"],"title":"時間追溯：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Temporal genealogy: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看最後一台設備便確定來源」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Blaming only the final tool.","instruction":"接續前一步「時間追溯」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看最後一台設備便確定來源」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：混批會破壞腔室追溯。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Temporal genealogy artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Blaming only the final tool\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Mixed lots can break chamber traceability. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力；混批會破壞腔室追溯。","observationEn":"Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone; Mixed lots can break chamber traceability.","failure":"若採用「只看最後一台設備便確定來源」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Blaming only the final tool\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「時間追溯」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「混批會破壞腔室追溯」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Temporal genealogy, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Mixed lots can break chamber traceability\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-16-k1","title":"時間追溯／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temporal genealogy / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：混批會破壞腔室追溯。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Mixed lots can break chamber traceability."},{"id":"a094-v8-16-k2","title":"時間追溯／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temporal genealogy / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看最後一台設備便確定來源」與「共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Blaming only the final tool\" is not equivalent to \"Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「時間追溯」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Temporal genealogy?","options":["混批會破壞腔室追溯","只看最後一台設備便確定來源","直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數"],"optionsEn":["Mixed lots can break chamber traceability","Blaming only the final tool","Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders"],"answer":0,"explanation":"混批會破壞腔室追溯；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mixed lots can break chamber traceability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-16"],"title":"缺陷增量：建立模型","titleEn":"Defect adders: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions.","instruction":"配對前後圖並保留消失、移動與新增三種情況。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Pair pre/post maps and separate disappearing, moved and new detections. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比；靈敏度不同可產生假的增量。","observationEn":"Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions; Sensitivity differences create false adders.","failure":"若採用「直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「缺陷增量」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比。","checkEn":"Submit the Defect adders diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-17-k1","title":"缺陷增量／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defect adders / Physics and model","text":"機制：新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比。","textEn":"Mechanism: Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions."},{"id":"a094-v8-17-k2","title":"缺陷增量／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defect adders / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「缺陷增量」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Defect adders, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測","新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比","直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數"],"optionsEn":["Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone","Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions","Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders"],"answer":1,"explanation":"新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-17"],"title":"缺陷增量：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Defect adders: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders.","instruction":"接續前一步「缺陷增量」成果，先指出錯誤主張「直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：靈敏度不同可產生假的增量。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Defect adders artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Sensitivity differences create false adders. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比；靈敏度不同可產生假的增量。","observationEn":"Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions; Sensitivity differences create false adders.","failure":"若採用「直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「缺陷增量」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「靈敏度不同可產生假的增量」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Defect adders, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Sensitivity differences create false adders\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-18-k1","title":"缺陷增量／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defect adders / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：靈敏度不同可產生假的增量。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Sensitivity differences create false adders."},{"id":"a094-v8-18-k2","title":"缺陷增量／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defect adders / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數」與「新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders\" is not equivalent to \"Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「缺陷增量」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Defect adders?","options":["直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數","任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測","靈敏度不同可產生假的增量"],"optionsEn":["Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders","Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone","Sensitivity differences create false adders"],"answer":2,"explanation":"靈敏度不同可產生假的增量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sensitivity differences create false adders. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a094-stage04","order":4,"title":"良率模型 → 改善驗證","titleEn":"Yield model to Improvement verification","description":"把「良率模型」「電性關聯」「改善驗證」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Yield model, Electrical correlation, Improvement verification.","steps":[{"id":"a094-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-18"],"title":"良率模型：建立模型","titleEn":"Yield model: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects.","instruction":"用假設隨機獨立缺陷比較 Y=exp(-AD0) 與聚集情況。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設致命缺陷為空間獨立均勻 Poisson 過程，晶粒面積 A=1 cm²、缺陷密度 D0=0.1 cm⁻²，零缺陷良率 Y=exp(−AD0)=exp(−0.1)≈90.48%。面積加倍時 Y≈81.87%。聚集缺陷、冗餘修復與參數失效不在模型內，不能當實廠良率預測。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical Poisson yield with clustered defects. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume spatially independent uniform Poisson killer defects with die area A=1 cm² and density D0=0.1 cm⁻². Zero-defect yield Y=exp(−AD0)=exp(−0.1)≈90.48%; doubling area gives 81.87%. Clustering, repair redundancy and parametric failures are excluded; this is not a fab-yield prediction.","observation":"Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設；聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群。","observationEn":"Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects; Cluster models can suit some defect populations.","failure":"若採用「任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「良率模型」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設。\n算例驗收：驗算兩個良率，確認 AD0 無單位，並說明良率並非隨面積線性下降。","checkEn":"Submit the Yield model diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify both yields, confirm dimensionless AD0 and explain why yield does not decrease linearly with area.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-19-k1","title":"良率模型／物理與模型","titleEn":"Yield model / Physics and model","text":"機制：Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設。","textEn":"Mechanism: Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects."},{"id":"a094-v8-19-k2","title":"良率模型／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Yield model / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測」。\n假設數值與推算：假設致命缺陷為空間獨立均勻 Poisson 過程，晶粒面積 A=1 cm²、缺陷密度 D0=0.1 cm⁻²，零缺陷良率 Y=exp(−AD0)=exp(−0.1)≈90.48%。面積加倍時 Y≈81.87%。聚集缺陷、冗餘修復與參數失效不在模型內，不能當實廠良率預測。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume spatially independent uniform Poisson killer defects with die area A=1 cm² and density D0=0.1 cm⁻². Zero-defect yield Y=exp(−AD0)=exp(−0.1)≈90.48%; doubling area gives 81.87%. Clustering, repair redundancy and parametric failures are excluded; this is not a fab-yield prediction."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「良率模型」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Yield model, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設","任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測","影像分類即可取代電性驗證"],"optionsEn":["Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects","Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone","Replacing electrical validation with image classification"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-19"],"title":"良率模型：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Yield model: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「良率模型」成果，先指出錯誤主張「任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Yield model artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Cluster models can suit some defect populations. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設；聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群。","observationEn":"Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects; Cluster models can suit some defect populations.","failure":"若採用「任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「良率模型」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Yield model, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Cluster models can suit some defect populations\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-20-k1","title":"良率模型／物理與模型","titleEn":"Yield model / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Cluster models can suit some defect populations."},{"id":"a094-v8-20-k2","title":"良率模型／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Yield model / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測」與「Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone\" is not equivalent to \"Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「良率模型」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Yield model?","options":["影像分類即可取代電性驗證","聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群","任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測"],"optionsEn":["Replacing electrical validation with image classification","Cluster models can suit some defect populations","Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cluster models can suit some defect populations. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-20"],"title":"電性關聯：建立模型","titleEn":"Electrical correlation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Not every visible defect has electrical impact.","instruction":"交叉列出視覺缺陷與電性失效，保留無對應案例。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Cross-tab visual defects/electrical failures and retain unmatched cases. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響；電性測試也有漏檢與誤警。","observationEn":"Not every visible defect has electrical impact; Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects.","failure":"若採用「影像分類即可取代電性驗證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Replacing electrical validation with image classification\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電性關聯」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響。","checkEn":"Submit the Electrical correlation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Not every visible defect has electrical impact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-21-k1","title":"電性關聯／物理與模型","titleEn":"Electrical correlation / Physics and model","text":"機制：不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響。","textEn":"Mechanism: Not every visible defect has electrical impact."},{"id":"a094-v8-21-k2","title":"電性關聯／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Electrical correlation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「影像分類即可取代電性驗證」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Replacing electrical validation with image classification."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電性關聯」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Electrical correlation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["影像分類即可取代電性驗證","降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低","不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響"],"optionsEn":["Replacing electrical validation with image classification","Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction","Not every visible defect has electrical impact"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Not every visible defect has electrical impact. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-21"],"title":"電性關聯：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Electrical correlation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「影像分類即可取代電性驗證」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Replacing electrical validation with image classification.","instruction":"接續前一步「電性關聯」成果，先指出錯誤主張「影像分類即可取代電性驗證」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電性測試也有漏檢與誤警。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Electrical correlation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Replacing electrical validation with image classification\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響；電性測試也有漏檢與誤警。","observationEn":"Not every visible defect has electrical impact; Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects.","failure":"若採用「影像分類即可取代電性驗證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Replacing electrical validation with image classification\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電性關聯」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電性測試也有漏檢與誤警」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Electrical correlation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-22-k1","title":"電性關聯／物理與模型","titleEn":"Electrical correlation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電性測試也有漏檢與誤警。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects."},{"id":"a094-v8-22-k2","title":"電性關聯／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Electrical correlation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「影像分類即可取代電性驗證」與「不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Replacing electrical validation with image classification\" is not equivalent to \"Not every visible defect has electrical impact\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電性關聯」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Electrical correlation?","options":["電性測試也有漏檢與誤警","影像分類即可取代電性驗證","降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低"],"optionsEn":["Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects","Replacing electrical validation with image classification","Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電性測試也有漏檢與誤警；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-22"],"title":"改善驗證：建立模型","titleEn":"Improvement verification: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement.","instruction":"用時間分割對照檢查修正前後缺陷和良率，固定檢出設定。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Use time-separated controls with fixed detection settings. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善；改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合。","observationEn":"Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement; Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes.","failure":"若採用「降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「改善驗證」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善。","checkEn":"Submit the Improvement verification diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-23-k1","title":"改善驗證／物理與模型","titleEn":"Improvement verification / Physics and model","text":"機制：檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善。","textEn":"Mechanism: Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement."},{"id":"a094-v8-23-k2","title":"改善驗證／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Improvement verification / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「改善驗證」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Improvement verification, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數","檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善","降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低"],"optionsEn":["Equating detection count with failed-die count","Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement","Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-23"],"title":"改善驗證：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Improvement verification: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction.","instruction":"接續前一步「改善驗證」成果，先指出錯誤主張「降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Improvement verification artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善；改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合。","observationEn":"Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement; Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes.","failure":"若採用「降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「改善驗證」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Improvement verification, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-24-k1","title":"改善驗證／物理與模型","titleEn":"Improvement verification / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes."},{"id":"a094-v8-24-k2","title":"改善驗證／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Improvement verification / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低」與「檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction\" is not equivalent to \"Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「改善驗證」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Improvement verification?","options":["降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低","把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數","改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合"],"optionsEn":["Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction","Equating detection count with failed-die count","Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes"],"answer":2,"explanation":"改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"metrology","subcategoryTitle":"量測、良率與控制","subcategoryTitleEn":"Metrology, yield and control"}};
